To use the Virtual Fly Brain Model Context Protocol (MCP) tool, follow these steps:
Open Claude Desktop and go to Settings, navigate to the MCP section, add a new MCP server with the specified settings, and restart Claude Code for changes to take effect.
Alternatively, use the Configuration JSON or Claude Code Setup methods.

For GitHub Copilot Setup, open VS Code with GitHub Copilot installed, open Settings, search for "MCP" in the settings search, find the MCP Servers setting, add the server URL, and give it a name like "Virtual Fly Brain".
For other MCP-compatible clients, use the provided JSON configuration.
For Gemini Setup, connect through custom Python/Node.js clients that support MCP, and use the mcp and google-genai libraries to connect.

```json
{
"mcpServers": {
 "virtual-fly-brain": {
 "type": "http",
 "url": "https://vfb3-mcp.virtualflybrain.org",
 "tools": ["*"]
 }
}
}
```
